    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1955-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Inverse-square variation gives \\(y=\\frac{k}{x^2}.\\) Since \\(16=\\frac{k}{1^2},\\) we have \\(k=16.\\) At \\(x=8,\\) \\[ y=\\frac{16}{8^2}=\\frac14. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Write the variation as \\(y=\\frac{k}{x^2}\\)",
        "Use the first pair of values to determine \\(k\\)"
      ],
